    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nIt is already possible to set an `abbr_hlgroup` to customize the `abbr` in complete-items (https://github.com/neovim/neovim/commit/ed3fb1bb9ad97435c50655ee8de71b2d7d67d01c) , but it would be really nice if we could support range highlight using extmark for this.\n\nThis would allow for some really nice customization of the completion menu, and making something like this: https://github.com/xzbdmw/colorful-menu.nvim possible to use for the builtin completion menu.\n\nNot sure if it also then makes sense to have extmark highlights for `kind` and `menu` as well then if we decide to add it to `abbr`(?)\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nSomething like `abbr_highlights` (or another name) that is a list of extmark highlights where one could specify the start and end col of the highlight.",
    "closed_at": null,
    "closed_by": null,
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> but it would be really nice if we could support range highlight using extmark for this.\n\nemm  popupmenu is not a buffer. \n\n> Not sure if it also then makes sense to have extmark highlights for kind and menu as well then if we decide to add it to abbr(?)\n\ncomplete-items also have `kind_hlgroup` and `PmenuExtara` for menu text.  \n\nI checked out this plugin. The only difference is that it uses extmarks on abbr to do syntax highlighting. For completion... I don’t feel there’s much benefit. Too much highlighting isn’t good for eyes either. \n\n",
            "created_at": "2026-09-17T08:41:30Z",
