        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> Should it be? :)\n\nnah, don't think it has to be. what we actually need is just range highlights on abbr — `pumitem_T` can carry a list of `{start, end, hl}` and `pum_redraw()` paints them. the marktree wouldn't buy us anything here anyway, items get rebuilt on every keystroke.\n\nfor the colorful-menu case the plugin already does the hard part on its side: treesitter can parse a plain string, so it highlights the label, collects the captures as byte ranges and just hands them over via something like `abbr_highlights`. we'd only need to paint them, and `kind`/`menu` would come for free. the annoying bit is abbr goes through `transstr()` (and `reverse_text()` for rl) before drawing, so the cols need remapping.\n\nwill try it after new completion model..\n",
            "created_at": "2026-09-18T11:46:16Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/41947#issuecomment-5729519479",
